
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>CSS Box Model - Annotated</title>

    <style>
        * {
            box-sizing: content-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f1f5f9;
            color: #1e293b;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        header {
            text-align: center;
            background-color: #2563eb;
            color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #1e40af;
        }

        /* Margin: Space outside the border */
        .box {
            margin: 30px;
            /* Padding: Space between content and border */
            padding: 20px;
            /* Border: Surrounds the padding and content */
            border: 5px solid #2563eb;
            /* Content: The actual text area */
            background-color: #bfdbfe;
        }

        .content {
            background-color: #fde68a;
            padding: 15px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .margin-example {
            margin: 40px;
            padding: 20px;
            border: 4px solid #059669;
            background-color: #d1fae5;
        }

        .padding-example {
            margin: 20px;
            padding: 40px;
            border: 3px solid #dc2626;
            background-color: #fee2e2;
        }

        .border-example {
            margin: 20px;
            padding: 15px;
            border: 10px dashed #7c3aed;
            background-color: #ede9fe;
        }

        .diagram {
            background-color: #fef3c7;
            border: 2px dashed #d97706;
            padding: 20px;
            text-align: center;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }

        .diagram-border {
            background-color: #bfdbfe;
            border: 5px solid #2563eb;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .diagram-content {
            background-color: #fde68a;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            background-color: #1e293b;
            color: white;
            padding: 15px;
            margin-top: 30px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <header>
        <h1>CSS Box Model</h1>
        <p>Understanding Content, Padding, Border and Margin</p>
    </header>

    <main>

        <section>
            <h2>1. Box Model Overview</h2>
            <p>Every HTML element is represented as a rectangular box.</p>

            <div class="diagram">
                <strong>Margin</strong> - Space outside the border

                <div class="diagram-border">
                    <strong>Border</strong> - Surrounds the padding and content

                    <div class="diagram-content">
                        <strong>Padding</strong> - Space around the content

                        <div class="content">
                            <strong>Content</strong>
                            <p>Text or other elements appear here.</p>
                        </div>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>2. Complete Box Example</h2>

            <div class="box">
                <div class="content">
                    This is the content area.
                </div>
                <p>Padding: 20px</p>
                <p>Border: 5px solid blue</p>
                <p>Margin: 30px</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>3. Margin Example</h2>
            <p>Margin creates space outside an element's border.</p>

            <div class="margin-example">
                This box has a margin of 40px.
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>4. Padding Example</h2>
            <p>Padding creates space between content and border.</p>

            <div class="padding-example">
                This box has a padding of 40px.
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>5. Border Example</h2>
            <p>Border surrounds the content and padding.</p>

            <div class="border-example">
                This box has a 10px dashed purple border.
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>6. Box Size Calculation</h2>

            <p>For the default content-box model:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Content width = 200px</li>
                <li>Left and right padding = 20px each</li>
                <li>Left and right border = 5px each</li>
                <li>Left and right margin = 30px each</li>
            </ul>

            <p><strong>Total width including margin:</strong></p>
            <p>200 + 40 + 10 + 60 = 310px</p>

            <p>
                The visible box width, excluding margin, is
                200 + 40 + 10 = 250px.
            </p>
        </section>

    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 | CSS Box Model Learning Project</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
